[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":38},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-7,"_20":21,"_22":-7,"_23":24,"_25":26},"tipo","etapa","cubo",{"_11":35,"_13":36,"_28":37},"id","pontas-e-centros","nome","Tips and centers","rascunho",false,"html","<p>The way to solve the Pyraminx for the first time: by layers, as on the cube. First the tips and the centers, which take a few turns and no algorithm; then the 3 bottom edges; last the 3 top ones. Read it with the Pyraminx in your hand.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0df28df0478ed6e0.svg\" alt=\"The solved Pyraminx, the way you will hold it: one tip up, green in front.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The solved Pyraminx, the way you will hold it: one tip up, green in front.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/25128eed4c8b0628.svg\" alt=\"From below: the yellow face.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>From below: the yellow face.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<h2>The pieces</h2>\n<p>The Pyraminx has three kinds of piece:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Tips (4)</strong>: the little points. They turn on their own and don&#39;t move anything else.</li>\n<li><strong>Centers (4)</strong>: right below each tip, with 3 colors. They never leave their place: they only turn, together with the tip above them.</li>\n<li><strong>Edges (6)</strong>: between two tips, with 2 colors. These are the ones that take work.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/bdf8c25f9f3101fe.svg\" alt=\"The 4 tips.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The 4 tips.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/793cb63cd4949a97.svg\" alt=\"The tips and the centers: each center right below its tip.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The tips and the centers: each center right below its tip.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<h2>How to hold it</h2>\n<p>Throughout the method, hold the Pyraminx with one tip up and the yellow face on the bottom. Start with green in front: red is on the left and blue on the right.</p>\n<p>The turns are named after the tip, looking at it: <code>U</code> (the top one), <code>L</code> (the left one, in front), <code>R</code> (the right one, in front) and <code>B</code> (the back one). The capital letter turns the tip and the layer below it; the lowercase one (<code>u</code>, <code>l</code>, <code>r</code>, <code>b</code>), just the tip. On its own, the letter is 1/3 of a turn clockwise; with an apostrophe (<code>R&#39;</code>), counterclockwise. All the turns are on the <a href=\"/en/pyraminx/notation\">notation page</a>, with a diagram for each one.</p>\n<h2>Step 1: the tips</h2>\n<p>Each tip has 3 colors, and so does the center right below it. Turn the tip (with the lowercase letter) until its colors match the center&#39;s. A tip has only 3 positions: at most 2 turns.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\"><ol aria-label=\"r\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/583781c00be9a404-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>r</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/583781c00be9a404-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>The right tip didn&#39;t match its center: <code>r</code> fixes it.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>Do this on all 4 tips. From now on they turn together with the centers and stay right.</p>\n<h2>Step 2: the centers</h2>\n<p>A center is right when its colors match the other centers, face by face. To turn a center, use the capital letter: the center turns together with its tip, and the two keep matching.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>The 3 bottom centers</strong> (those of the <code>L</code>, <code>R</code> and <code>B</code> tips): turn each one until its yellow is on the bottom. The other colors fall into place on their own.</li>\n<li><strong>The top center</strong>: turn <code>U</code> until its 3 colors match the faces.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\"><ol aria-label=\"L\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/8960bab83df3827b-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>L</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/8960bab83df3827b-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>The left center with its yellow off the bottom: <code>L</code> brings the yellow down.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama tira\"><ol aria-label=\"U'\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/30f27faf92f9ebad-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>U'</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/30f27faf92f9ebad-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>The top center, seen from above: <code>U&#39;</code> lines up its colors with the faces.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>Done: the tips and the centers. Each face already has its color on the 3 centers; now the edges are left.</p>\n","treino","metodos",[30],"anterior","proximo",{"_13":27,"_28":29},"grupos",[],"1st layer","endereco","/pyraminx/primeira-camada",{"_13":31,"_32":33,"_28":34},"Top-first","numero",1,"/pyraminx/top-first#pontas-e-centros","pyraminx","Pyraminx","/pyraminx/",{"_39":40,"_41":42},"cubos",[45,46,47,48,49,50,51],"idiomas",[43,44],"pt","en",{"_11":59,"_13":59},{"_11":58,"_13":58},{"_11":57,"_13":57},{"_11":56,"_13":56},{"_11":54,"_13":55},{"_11":35,"_13":36},{"_11":52,"_13":53},"skewb","Skewb","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","2x2","3x3"]
